        "self_reported": {
          "assumptions": [
            "shlex.split reading the old `argv: $*` form is safe because no landed argv token carries a quote, backslash, $, backtick or #; tests/test_recordings.py pins that for every carried paste in the tree",
            "the README command cell stays the unquoted form (bale + argv joined by single spaces) for new landings too, since the landed rows are that form and --check compares rows exactly",
            "the real recorder cannot be run here (no bale on PATH, no ~/twine-src); the harness runs it against a stub bale, which reaches every rec call and the environment section but not the crafter's three recordings",
            "twine/commands/carry_bale.py is left untouched even though one docstring line there is now stale (outside the four named twine/ files)"
          ],
          "judgment_calls": [
            "module name twine/probing.py (R3's suggestion); it also took Outcome, CarryOutcome, CARRIED_KINDS and the limits, because the four helpers need them and the tool would otherwise still import carry.py for Outcome and DEFAULT_TIMEOUT_SECONDS",
            "helpers take a ProbeSeam (run, which, env, info) rather than a Context: a Protocol Context already satisfies, plus a small concrete Seam that collects info lines \u2014 so probe.py no longer builds a Context nor strips the '[twine] ' prefix; probe_context was renamed probe_seam (nothing else referenced it)",
            "carry.py re-exports the moved names (noqa F401 on the ones it does not call) instead of editing carry_bale.py and the tests that import them from there",
            "argv: is printed with printf 'argv:'; printf ' %q' \"$@\"; echo \u2014 no trailing space, so the lander's field reading and the shlex round trip need no strip",
            "the lander's command_cell is rebuilt from the parsed argv rather than echoed, so a quoted-form paste produces the same README rows as the old form",
            "an unbalanced quote in an echoed command is a ValueError (a Refusal in the lander), never a silent fallback to space-splitting",
            "tests/test_probing.py's import walk resolves relative imports and also counts `from twine import cli` / `from twine.commands import x`, which a plain module-name check would miss"
          ],
